  "ingredients": [
    "1/4 cup onion (grated)",
    "3 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "2 tablespoon fresh parsley (chopped)",
    "2 teaspoon paprika",
    "2 teaspoon cumin",
    "1/2 teaspoon ground coriander",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "16 ounce ground lamb",
    "6 ounce spring mix",
    "3 tablespoon olive oil",
    "3 tablespoon red wine vinegar",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "4 tablespoon feta cheese (crumbled)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Gather and prep all ingredients. If using wooden skewers, soak in water for 30 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, combine onion, garlic, parsley, cumin, paprika, and coriander.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir together the ingredients until everything is well combined.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add in the lamb, then season with salt and pepper. Lightly mix with your hands until everything is combined. Try your best not to over-mix.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide the meat into portions. Form the meat around the skewer, about 1 inch thick, in sections about 1 inch apart. You should get 2-3 sections of meat per skewer.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-heat your grill (or grill pan, if using a stove) to medium-high heat. Place skewers on the grill and cook for 2-3 minutes, then flip and cook for an additional 2-4 minutes depending on the doneness you want. Once done, remove from grill and wrap with foil.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-6.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "While meat is resting, create the salad. Whisk together olive oil, red wine vinegar, and salt and pepper to taste. You can add these to a mason jar and shake hard to combine if preferred. Dress the salad with dressing, then sprinkle feta cheese over the top.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Lamb-Kofta-with-Tangy-Salad-7.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve together and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lamb-kofta-with-side-salad/#wprm-recipe-54949-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
